# Power: the power switch cuts power with no warning. That is fine: switching
# off is a fresh start. Only the parents' max volume survives (hearing
# protection); Wi-Fi and Bluetooth pairings are kept by the system, not tapboxd.

# Clean shutdown (`poweroff`, an update): stop playing, show it on the LED.
tap story-440
wait 42s
power off
expect cmd pause
expect not cmd persist           # nothing about playback is written
expect led shutting-down

# Within one session, lifting and re-tapping resumes.
power cut
tap story-440
wait 30s
lift
tap story-440
expect cmd resume

# After a power cut: fresh start, default volume, from the beginning.
click vol-down
click vol-down
expect volume 30
power cut
expect idle
expect led idle
expect volume 40
tap story-440
expect cmd play
expect not cmd resume
lift

# Max volume set by a parent's card survives.
tap admin-vol-max-50
expect cmd persist
lift
power cut
expect max-volume 50
click vol-up
click vol-up
expect volume 50
